  "notes": "Cash-basis village. Governmental data from Statement of Receipts, Disbursements and Changes in Fund Balances (Total column, p4); General, Street, Keno are governmental. Water, Sewer, Sanitation are business-type (p6 total column). Interest income, bond principal/interest printed below the Total Receipts/Disbursements on p4 and the 'Other receipts (disbursements)' block on p6 are recorded as normal items with outside_printed_total. Business-type: 770,085 + 429,249 + 4,752 + 53,905 - 379,084 - 30,000 - 16,743 - 158,830 = 673,334 vs printed 673,333 (report is off by 1). Cash flow statement (pp7-8) shows beginning 770,084 vs 770,085 on p6; p6 used. Balance sheet is the government-wide cash basis Statement of Net Position, Total column (governmental -19,417 + proprietary 673,333 = 653,916). Governmental cash is negative (Street fund -116,873). General Fund statement on p9 shows the combined governmental totals (278,824 / 241,635) despite its title, so it is a duplicate and not recorded in detail. Budget schedule p10 mixes governmental and utility revenue in single lines (Taxes 299,348 includes water bond property tax), so its revenue lines are recorded as printed under fund 'All funds (budget schedule)' (fund_type by dominant/whole fund type, mixed lines marked review; Grants, donations and misc. is zero and omitted), plus its spending lines. Personnel services 114,714 on p4 is split by its printed General 71,354 / Street 43,360 columns. Charges for services 21,920 on p4 is the franchise fee (p10 'Franchise Fees', p2 'Electric, gas, and cable lease'), so it is recorded as occupation/franchise tax. Zero line Keno omitted. Budget schedule spending lines (Water/Sewer/Sanitation as departments) are under fund 'All funds (budget schedule)' with the printed TOTAL DISBURSEMENTS 934,924 (lines add to 934,923, rounding). Read pages 1-10 of 10"
